# Arguments for rezoagwe-discovery. See rezoagwe-discovery -h.
#
#   -bootstrap  seed address, or a comma-separated list
#   -node       address to bind
#   -advertise  address peers should use to reach this node
#   -nick       name shown in chat and peer lists
#   -cluster    cluster name; nodes only talk to their own cluster
#   -psk        pre-shared key authenticating every packet
#   -http       HTTP gateway address
#
# -advertise matters on anything but one machine: a node bound to ":3137" tells
# every peer to reach it at ":3137", which each of them resolves to its own
# loopback. Set it to an address that routes.
#
# The HTTP gateway is a full read/write control surface — POST /import?mode=seed
# rewrites the whole cluster. Bind it to loopback, or set -http-token and
# -http-tls-cert/-http-tls-key.
REZOAGWE_DISCOVERY_ARGS="-bootstrap 127.0.0.1:9999 -node :3137 -data /var/lib/rezoagwe/node.json"
